Problem 8.19
Explain why (CH_3)_3 \overset{\circ}{C} is more stable than CH_3 \overset{\circ}{C}H_2 and \overset{\circ}{C}H_3 is the least stable cation.
Solution
Hyperconjugation interaction in (CH_3)_3C is greater than in CH_3CH_2 as the (CH_3)_3C has nine C-H bonds. In \dot{C}H_3, vacant p orbital is perpendicular to the plane in which C-H bonds lie; hence cannot overlap with it. Thus, \dot{C}H_3 lacks hyperconjugative stability.

